+# Independent review request: 30000590
+
+Please audit the complete five-turn packet and exact source scope. The proposed original disposition is unsolved 5/5. No full proof, original counterexample or novelty claim is proposed.
+
+Start with SOURCE_SCOPE.md, SOURCE_LOCATOR_CORRECTION.md and RESULT.md, then read all five TURN files and the six bound primary PDFs where needed. The original OWR question is printed p.2590/PDF12. The right-module convention is explicit in the companion DDJO paper. Davis's FP definition is finite-length, with the filtered-colimit criterion after Theorem 3.3 in the PD survey. Sharifi's Theorem 4.3.12 is on printed/PDF97 of the bound download. The duality flatness condition is explicit in turn 4 and the Davis--Okun section 9 convention.
+
+Highest-risk obligations:
+
+- finite-index coinduction as a left G/right H bimodule, including nonnormal H, and both directions of finite generation;
+- top-syzygy FP_2 equivalence and the distinction between an arbitrary finite complex and a dual augmentation resolution;
+- ascending-HNN incidence map, stable-letter orientation, finite-height support and right equivariance;
+- integral Kunneth Tor degrees/naturality, field detection and Bockstein scopes;
+- normal-extension FP proof, the right G-action extending the usual right N-action, the explicit nonsplit bimodule isomorphism, Z-flat dualizing module and diagonal generation;
+- the countable height-kernel homology, opposite index shifts, faithful induction, actual matrix noncoherence and the positive ambient group's regular cohomology;
+- precise distinction from the earlier all-fields PD target and from known Coxeter/Artin/Bestvina--Brady positive cases.
+
+Please replay all controls and verify every frozen binding, but do not treat finite checks as proofs of the infinite claims. Report exact necessary corrections before final disposition. Any correction must be additive to the frozen historical packet. The full five-turn budget has been used; review is not a further author search.
