+# Second substantive author turn
+
+2026-10-02. The Bass–Serre mapping-cone resolution preserves typeFP for an
+ascending HNN extension. On base cohomology the stable-letter incidence map
+shifts a finite height grading, making identity minus transport injective
+even if transport has a kernel. The resulting cokernel is finitely generated
+whenever base group-ring cohomology is. An explicit BS(1,m) cyclic right-
+module presentation checks the formula in a non-surjective case. Finite
+free products also preserve the property.46,264 exact controls pass.
+Original unresolved2/5; subjective completion30%. Next investigate product
+Tor terms without repeating the distinct PD-over-fields problem.
