@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Third substantive author turn
+
+2026-10-02. Integral Kunneth isolates exactly the remaining Tor finite-
+generation requirement for a product of positive FP groups. One flat
+cohomology factor suffices; over a field the product property is equivalent
+to the two factor properties. Integral PD factors only shift the modules.
+Bockstein sequences identify fixed-modulus torsion kernels when integral
+finite generation is already assumed; no all-fields-to-integral inference
+or repetition of predecessor2579 is claimed.79,346 exact controls pass.
+Original unresolved3/5; subjective completion35%. Next: non-split normal
+extensions and a duality-quotient collapse of the spectral sequence.
