+# Substantive author turn 4
+
+Proved the normal-extension closure theorem by retaining the conjugation action through the quotient regular-bimodule identification. The inner-action prism, nonsplit lift cancellation, quotient flatness, finite-length FP closure and diagonal finite-generation argument are explicit. Exact finite controls check 9,324 noncommutative bar prisms and 18,225 nonsplit bimodule cases, among 83,797 assertions. The theorem uses standard spectral-sequence and duality inputs and is not claimed novel. Original target remains unresolved; one genuine author turn remains.
