+The target is finite generation of total H*(Gamma;ZGamma) as a **right ZGamma-module**, for groups virtually of type FP. FP here means a finite-length resolution by finitely generated projectives. Neither abelian-group finite generation nor a weaker FP-infinity hypothesis is substituted.
+
+The packet proves scoped finite-index and syzygy reductions, ascending-HNN/free-product positive results, integral product and fixed-torsion criteria, and extension closure with a Z-flat duality quotient. The last turn gives an explicit non-finitely-generated matrix kernel over Z[F2 times F2], while proving that this ambient group's own regular cohomology is finitely generated. The unresolved augmentation-resolution realization gap is essential. The flatness, actual Tor and height-support hypotheses have not been removed.
+
+A complete independent AI-assisted source/proof audit passed all five turns. It requested only a bibliographic page correction, supplied additively. This is not human peer review or historical novelty certification. Known Coxeter/Artin/Bestvina--Brady cases and standard homological methods are credited.
